p.src:
The speaker makes the test concrete with numbers. Suppose there are six risky variables and only two can be controlled. In our notation, $\begin{aligned}
n&=6, & c&=2, & u&=4,\\
\rho&=\frac{2}{6}=\frac{1}{3}.\end{aligned}$ The speaker’s judgment is that this is not a good idea. We should not take a flyer while admitting that most of the important variables are loose.

