p.src:
The two numerical examples preserve the core comparison: $\frac{2}{6}
\quad \text{is a weaker control position than} \quad
\frac{2}{3}.$ But the ratio is not the whole story. A disciplined entrepreneur also asks whether the remaining uncertainty fits personal risk tolerance, and whether the size of the bet matches the upside being pursued.

